   PlotInteractivity:>True,
   PlotLabel->FormBox[
     StyleBox[
     "\"Food Spawned/Timestep (1/T) vs Growth Rate\"", 16, Bold, StripOnInput -> 
      False], TraditionalForm],
   PlotRange->{{0., 10.}, {0., 0.244679649013198}},
   PlotRangeClipping->True,
   PlotRangePadding->{{
      Scaled[0.02], 
      Scaled[0.02]}, {
      Scaled[0.02], 
      Scaled[0.05]}},
   Ticks->{Automatic, Automatic}]], "Output",
  CellChangeTimes->{3.9887619355261154`*^9},ExpressionUUID->
  "c4853d09-33af-0045-a681-1cd325e0eabe"],
 "\n\nThat being said, the Food Spawned/Timestep (1/T) vs. Growth Rate did \
seem to have a somewhat positive relationship, however indeterminate. The \
growth rate was 0 for 1 Food Spawned/Timestep because the food was so low the \
population died off early. This relationship may be explained by the fact \
that more food allows agents to increase their energy reserves to the point \
where the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["reproductionCooldown",
   FontSlant->"Italic"]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "92b3a515-d37a-2143-a765-253418ccadfb"],
 " becomes the only limiting factor on reproduction and not the amount of \
energy agents have. In other words, as more food is available, agents meet \
basic survival needs and can then focus on reproduction with maximum \
efficiency."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9887631843877544`*^9, 3.9887633494022217`*^9}, {
  3.9887633940630436`*^9, 3.988763399952051*^9}},
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"5e2d5089-fd19-de4a-9a8f-3788feb64df0"]
}, Open  ]],

